# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# ProjectAssure — environment template (v23)
# Copy to `.env` for local runs, or add these in Vercel → Settings →
# Environment Variables. EVERY key is optional — the app degrades gracefully:
# no DATABASE_URL → per-user browser storage; no email keys → honest outbox;
# no AI keys → built-in deterministic intelligence engine.
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── 1 · DATABASE (recommended — enables per-user cloud persistence) ────────
# Any PostgreSQL provider works. Neon free tier is a good default:
#   https://neon.tech → create project → copy the pooled connection string.
# The correct Prisma schema (postgres vs sqlite) is picked automatically at
# install time — no file copying needed.
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# ── 2 · LIVE INTELLIGENCE (optional; any ONE, more = fallback chain) ───────
# Without these, the built-in deterministic engine answers (grounded, honest).
# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENAI_API_KEY=

# ── 3 · EMAIL DELIVERY (optional — real outbound email) ────────────────────
# Any ONE of these enables real email with attachments:
#   a) EMAIL_USER + EMAIL_PASS  — Gmail App Password (or any SMTP login)
#   b) BREVO_API_KEY            — https://app.brevo.com (300/day free)
#   c) RESEND_API_KEY           — https://resend.com (3,000/month free)
# EMAIL_USER=
# EMAIL_PASS=
# SMTP_HOST=smtp.gmail.com
# SMTP_PORT=465
# BREVO_API_KEY=
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# ALERT_EMAIL_FROM=

# ── 4 · HOST CONTROL (the separate admin deployment) ────────────────────────
# host-control/.env
# HOST_ADMIN_EMAIL=cpo@yourdomain.gov.in     # host portal login email
# HOST_ADMIN_PASSWORD=change-me-please       # host portal login password
# MAIN_PROJECT_URL=https://your-main-app.vercel.app   # what it polls
# Optional shared secret for main ↔ host traffic (set on BOTH apps):
# SYNC_TOKEN=
# AUTH_SECRET=                                # optional: signs user-state tokens
